1
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,960
Damn it all! This is bad!

2
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,240
I have to let Yoshikage know!

3
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:11,000
It's Reimi!

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,277
Hey Rohan, did you take
the pictures in this album?

5
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,380
I did, why?

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,897
I assume there's a reason
this one is marked.

7
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,417
What's so special about it?

8
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,147
You seem to have homed
in on this little boy.

9
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:24,650
Oh yeah.

10
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:26,384
I'm not too concerned with him.

11
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,897
He seemed to be sneaking around the
area so I thought I'd document him.

12
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:33,580
But look, the boy's
name is Hayato Kawajiri.

13
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,240
He has the same surname as this man.

14
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:40,120
Really? He does? Yeah. Check it out.

15
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,835
Weren't you investigating this person?

16
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,110
Mm-hmm.

17
00:00:44,193 --> 00:00:46,440
He was one of many potential suspects.

18
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,460
If Rohan Kishibe uncovers the truth,
it's over for my darling Yoshikage!

19
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,100
Hayato! Hayato!

20
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:00,950
Damn it.

21
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,537
This is the last time I'll say it, Hayato!

22
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:06,149
Answer me when I call you!

23
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,960
Oh, it's you, dear.

24
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,317
Sorry for all the commotion.

25
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,797
I could have sworn it
was Hayato in the bath.

26
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:18,117
Honestly, what are we
going to do with that boy?

27
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,197
Look at this place.

28
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:21,897
His clothes are scattered around
the hallway like a bomb went off.

29
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:23,837
I wish he'd take after
you a little bit more.

30
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:25,332
He could be such a slob.

31
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,342
Not to mention he's ignoring me.

32
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:32,357
Though if I know him, he's probably
reading manga with his headphones on again.

33
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,675
Honey, what happened?

34
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:35,881
You've got blood on your fingers.

35
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:37,460
Let me take care of that.

36
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,640
You don't want it to get infected.

37
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,342
No, I'll take care of it myself.

38
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,960
I just need a simple bandage.

39
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:48,360
I can handle that.

40
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:49,770
Oh.

41
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,197
I just caught my fingers in the door.

42
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,751
It's no big deal, really.

43
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:52,697
I'll see you

44
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:56,820
next time.

45
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:18,870
Good days!

46
00:03:18,953 --> 00:03:23,120
Good days!

47
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:29,700
Hayato Kawajiri?

48
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,637
So you think this grade school
kid has something to do with Kira?

49
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:36,777
Well, at this point, we're not
totally sure if they're connected.

50
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:39,860
That said, Rohan-sensei
thinks he's onto something.

51
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,800
I agree.

52
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:43,457
A grade school kid taking
videos of his dad on

53
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:46,017
the down low sends up
some serious red flags.

54
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,417
We're talking about meeting
up tomorrow morning.

55
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,817
Once we've gone through everything,

56
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,457
we'll head over to Hayato
Kawajiri's house together.

57
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:55,775
Rohan-sensei said he's already
figured out the address.

58
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,944
That artsy asshole doesn't
miss a beat, does he?

59
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,279
Well, count me in.

60
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,498
Oh, and I should ask Okuyasu, right?

61
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,860
And Jotaro, too.

62
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,653
Can't forget about him.

63
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,777
You can leave getting in touch with Mr.

64
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,690
Jotaro to me.

65
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,237
All right, we'll see you
tomorrow at 8.30 a .m.

66
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,017
Just look for the big Pepsi sign.

67
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,060
Right, got it.

68
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,240
Pepsi at 8.30.

69
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,873
That means I'm gonna be late for school.

70
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:23,880
Even so, if things pan out the way Rohan
hopes, it'll be worth the tardy slip.

71
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,540
Are you okay?

72
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,957
I can tell there's
something wrong, sweetie.

73
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,628
You're all pale and sweaty.

74
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:37,830
It's nothing.

75
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,078
I'm perfectly fine.

76
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,886
I'm just in some pain is all.

77
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:42,608
I did just slam my fingers.

78
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:45,660
Now please, go downstairs
and make some tea.

79
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,691
I'll be right behind you.

80
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,300
Okay, dear.

81
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:58,300
I know this is gonna sound totally
random, but well, I don't know.

82
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:01,407
You've had this vibe
like you'll live forever

83
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,609
The tea will be ready soon

84
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:19,357
If you so much as lay a single
finger on me your whole cover

85
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:23,028
will be blown sky-high Stay the
hell away from me and my mom!

86
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,177
It's non-negotiable, you got that?

87
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:27,201
Stay away or I reveal everything!

88
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,380
You're adorably naive!

89
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,120
As if I'd let someone find me out!

90
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:42,477
Getting rid of that Hayato brat
was the very height of foolishness!

91
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,597
You of all people should have known that!

92
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:47,197
Quiet, I'm trying to think
of a way out of this!

93
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,927
Don't waste time, it's
too late for that now!

94
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:54,757
You did a remarkable job of making it
look as though he fell and hit his head.

95
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,197
But your timing really
couldn't have been worse.

96
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:01,456
Rohan Kishibe has already begun his
investigation into Hayato Kawajiri.

97
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:05,620
They don't know for sure yet that
Kosaku Kawajiri is Yoshikage Kira.

98
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,447
But they're coming here tomorrow
to find out once and for all.

99
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,817
Sanyu mustn't remain in
this house a minute longer.

100
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,117
Will you stop talking?

101
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,376
I'm trying to think.

102
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,757
Even when you were a boy,

103
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:27,017
when things didn't go your way and
you felt the world was against you,

104
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:30,394
you'd always bite your nails
till your fingers were raw.

105
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,520
My poor sweet boy.

106
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:36,420
Oh, the misery you must be suffering.

107
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,277
We've run out of options here, kiddo.

108
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,301
You must leave this wretched
town behind for good.

109
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:49,781
If you get out now, you still have a chance
to escape and hold on to your anonymity.

110
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:55,220
Are you seriously asking me to
run away and abandon Morioh?

111
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:58,437
Living every moment in
excruciating secrecy is one of

112
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:01,077
the most horrible experiences
a person can go through,

113
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:03,336
and I refuse to go back to that hell.

114
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,420
I swear I will never leave this town.

115
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,380
What the hell?

116
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:19,617
The arrow moved on its own, but
I swear I didn't do anything.

117
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,640
I wasn't even touching it!

118
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:25,480
What's it doing?

119
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,480
No! Yoshikage!

120
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,880
Hiato! Hiato!

121
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,080
Just how long are you gonna sleep in?

122
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,320
It's time to get up and...

123
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:56,817
Hayato, why didn't you tell
me you were out of bed?

124
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:57,960
You startled me.

125
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:01,680
Come down for breakfast
and answer when I call you.

126
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,720
I had a terrible night's sleep.

127
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:14,322
That jerk-faced imposter found out I
witnessed one of his murders and assaulted me.

128
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:18,077
For now, I've made sure he can't
do anything to hurt me or mom.

129
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,042
But that's a temporary solution.

130
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,866
He'll find a way around that.

131
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:43,700
I don't understand!

132
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:46,985
What in the world's gotten
into you, Yoshikage?

133
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:50,928
You've been acting
strange since last night.

134
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,600
Don't ignore me!

135
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:58,682
I don't know why, but Rohan Kishibe is now
keen on snooping around Hayato Kawajiri.

136
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,548
We've run out of time, son.

137
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:03,268
They're coming to search
the house tomorrow.

138
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,250
Hmm.

139
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:05,780
There's no cause for alarm.

140
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,680
But Yoshikage!

141
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:14,260
My deadly queen has
acquired a third ability.

142
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:15,750
Huh?

143
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:23,480
What's going on here?

144
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:28,718
What could have happened to make you
so lackadaisical all of a sudden?

145
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,900
Miso-marinated cow tongue.

146
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:35,142
You're kidding.

147
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:37,655
Why didn't you say we were on the air?

148
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,100
Good morning, all.

149
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:40,440
It's 7.55.

150
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:43,408
Time for today's
prefectural weather report.

151
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:47,160
Today, we'll be enjoying
sunny skies. Hi-ya, Toe.

152
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,257
Hayato, are you listening?

153
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:50,340
Answer the phone!

154
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:56,026
His attitude has completely
changed since that bath last night.

155
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,519
What happened between now and then?

156
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,748
Hayato, what are you doing?

157
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:05,900
The damn phone isn't gonna
answer itself, you know!

158
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:11,680
My favorite China tea set!

159
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,460
This is all your fault!

160
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:15,977
Why do you ignore me?

161
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:18,017
Don't you have any
respect for your mother?

162
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:18,930
Admit it!

163
00:10:19,013 --> 00:10:21,317
You only see me as a
nuisance who gets in the way!

164
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,920
Well, fine! I'm done!

165
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:25,610
Now, now.

166
00:10:25,693 --> 00:10:28,032
Let's not start the day with an argument.

167
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:31,045
If it can't be fixed,
I'll buy you another one.

168
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:33,320
This is the Kawajiri residence.

169
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:36,120
No, I'm afraid not.

170
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,640
It was the wrong number, that's all.

171
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,852
And Hayato's going through a quiet phase.

172
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:42,981
No need to fret.

173
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,640
We're a family.

174
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:48,837
We should support each other,
not tear each other down.

175
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:50,273
Let's all work on that.

176
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,956
Speaking of work, I should get going.

177
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,860
But before I head off,
I'd like to steal a kiss.

178
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,200
Have a nice day.

179
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,760
Thank God, he took off.

180
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,120
No, I'm right here.

181
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,460
Why don't we walk together for a bit?

182
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:35,373
One moment I'm in the throes of despair.

183
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:37,307
Now I'm on top of the world.

184
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:39,716
So much has happened so very quickly.

185
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:42,389
It's been an absolute
whirlwind of emotion.

186
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:47,600
But now, at long last, I'll be able to
live a life free of worry and anxiety.

187
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:52,391
You really put the pressure on last
night, but because of you, I've matured.

188
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:57,980
You were so extraordinarily determined,
especially for a tank your age.

189
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:01,240
It's incredible that you
threatened Yoshikage Kira.

190
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:03,570
What?

191
00:12:03,653 --> 00:12:04,483
Yoshikage Kira?

192
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,259
Looks like I just told you my name.

193
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,757
Does this mean you're
going to kill me after all?

194
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,670
Kill you?

195
00:12:11,753 --> 00:12:13,720
Simply because you know my secret?

196
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,671
There's no need for that.

197
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,960
Like I said, I've matured.

198
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:21,105
It doesn't matter what
you or anyone else does.

199
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,496
No one in the world can rival me now.

200
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,720
You no longer arouse any interest in me.

201
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:32,017
And if I wanted to kill you, I would
have simply finished the job last night.

202
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:35,760
We're all going to get along
just fine, I guarantee it.

203
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,620
So take a breath, kiddo.

204
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:38,680
We're family.

205
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:43,320
Well, Daddy Dearest is off to the station.

206
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,936
Do your best at school today, Hayato.

207
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:52,680
No one can rival him?

208
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,270
Rival?

209
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:57,097
That means there must be
other people walking around

210
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,897
out there with the same
kind of bizarre powers.

211
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:02,240
Still, his confidence is terrifying.

212
00:13:02,580 --> 00:13:05,220
He's brazenly calling
himself unrivaled now.

213
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,153
Does that mean he gained some new power?

214
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,980
What do I do now?

215
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:12,500
Damn it!

216
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:15,080
I have no idea what I'm supposed to do!

217
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:23,140
Hey, you're Hayato Kawajiri. Huh?

218
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:25,420
Aren't you?

219
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,060
I've been waiting for you.

220
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:39,434
My name is Rohan Kishibe, and
I have a question for you.

221
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,741
Do us both a favor and answer it.

222
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,120
It's about this picture.

223
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,660
This is you, isn't it?

224
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,664
And you were taking a video of
your dad in the back there, right?

225
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,550
Wait.

226
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,280
What is this?

227
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,800
I know that was unexpected.

228
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,797
Questioning him would be troublesome.

229
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:05,577
Reading his mind will be much more
efficient when it comes to this endeavor!

230
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:08,900
Not to mention it'll be far
more accurate than a Q A?

231
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,110
Huh?

232
00:14:12,193 --> 00:14:13,944
Why would that be in his pages?

233
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:17,957
The only thing Heaven's Door
should be revealing is a candid,

234
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:23,300
honest, written account of this boy's
life memories And yet, there's a warning?

235
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:24,860
What's going on?

236
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:28,991
This warning here, is it part
of the boy's life experience?

237
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:34,137
When I drove over today, I wasn't planning
on giving him more than a quick peruse.

238
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:36,420
But now he's got me strangely hooked.

239
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,160
Do not read on. Hmm.

240
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,464
I wonder who that could be for.

241
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:53,917
What is all this?

242
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,720
This makes even less sense.

243
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:56,999
What does it mean?

244
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:00,980
Damn it all

245
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,380
This kid who the hell is he?

246
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:18,000
Come on the weather report
never said anything about rain

247
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:27,680
No way, a 27.

248
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:40,720
Who is this Hayato Kawajiri, and
how does he experience the future?

249
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:44,100
Could he be a stand user?

250
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,100
Calm down.

251
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,117
No way this is a stand ability.

252
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,320
Heaven's Door can't read the future.

253
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:55,897
It just reveals what
one has seen and heard.

254
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:59,627
I'm certain the explanation would
be somewhere in these pages.

255
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,410
Kira.

